{"content": "# Race Conditions: A Simple Explanation\n\n## What It Is\n\nA **race condition** occurs when the correctness of a program depends on the *timing* or *order* in which threads (or processes) execute. If two or more threads access shared data **simultaneously** and at least one of them modifies it, the result can be unpredictable \u2014 like a race where whoever \"wins\" gets to write their value last.\n\n## A Concrete Example\n\nImagine a bank account with a balance of **$100**. Two threads try to withdraw money at the same time:\n\n```python\nimport threading\n\nbalance = 100  # Shared state\n\ndef withdraw(amount):\n    global balance\n    # 1. Read the current balance\n    current = balance\n", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.4744182564815773, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.4744182564815773}, {"token": "Think", "logprob": -2.381627652843882}, {"token": "Imagine", "logprob": -2.4941192605098976}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -2.787797544201304}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -3.042405698498179}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -3.0515533425411476}, {"token": "Hey", "logprob": -3.9597393014034523}, {"token": "Hi", "logprob": -4.519082639416148}, {"token": "Hello", "logprob": -5.373103711803843}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -5.542260740002085}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.49713859339564}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -6.645337674816538}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -7.233613584240366}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -7.397710416515757}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -7.619077298839976}, {"token": "Thinking", "logprob": -7.800250623424937}, {"token": "What", "logprob": -7.99665031214564}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -8.318833921154429}, {"token": "Ex", "logprob": -8.473279569347788}, {"token": "Ah", "logprob": -8.609534833630015}]}, {"token": " Race", "logprob": -0.06766810347242824, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " Race", "logprob": -0.06766810347242824}, {"token": " What", "logprob": -3.107934140459733}, {"token": " Understanding",