{"content": "Here is the detailed analysis of the time complexity of Quicksort in the best, average, and worst cases.\n\n### 1. Best Case: $O(n \\log n)$\n\n**Scenario:**\nThe best case occurs when the partitioning algorithm consistently divides the array into two sub-arrays of roughly equal size. This happens when the pivot chosen is the median of the current sub-array.\n\n**Logical Deduction:**\n1.  **Partitioning Cost:** In each step, the algorithm scans the array to partition it. This takes linear time, $O(n)$.\n2.  **Recursion Depth:** If the array is split in half at every step, the number of levels in the recursion tree is $\\log_2 n$.\n3.  **Total", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.9597684659536654, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.9597684659536654}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -1.137527636485892}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -2.3705827512319857}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -2.4168092526968294}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -3.079879931407767}, {"token": "Qu", "logprob": -3.5440866269644076}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -3.887334994273978}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -4.9975988187368685}, {"token": "Quick", "logprob": -5.748756579356986}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -5.965007952648001}, {"token": "Below", "logprob": -7.051946810680228}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -7.720710925060111}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -8.07010286231597}, {"token": "For", "logprob": -8.112086466747122}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -8.251035860973197}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.477955988841849}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -8.588566950755911}, {"token": "qu", "logprob": -8.70130174537261}, {"token": "*", "logprob": -8.756862811046439}, {"token": "Ass", "logprob": -8.765937022167044}]}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0011352865787586097, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0011352865787586097}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -6.9572109549137195}, {"token": " represents", "logprob": -9.08134311128579}, {"token": " provides"