{"content": "```bash\nfind . -name \"*.py\" -type f -exec wc -l {} + | tail -1\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- `find . -name \"*.py\" -type f` \u2014 finds all regular files with the `.py` extension under the current directory.\n- `-exec wc -l {} +` \u2014 runs `wc -l` on all found files in batches (more efficient than `\\;`).\n- `tail -1` \u2014 extracts the last line, which is the total count from `wc -l`.\n\n> **Note:** If no `.py` files exist, `wc -l` won't run and `tail -1` will output nothing. To handle that edge case, you can use:\n> ```bash\n", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.04806631720351007, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.04806631720351007}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -3.5466777673988226}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -5.469433962467182}, {"token": "find", "logprob": -5.531426607730854}, {"token": "`", "logprob": -5.978854357364643}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -6.15042227423476}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -6.785916506412494}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -7.323079287174213}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -7.785302340152729}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -7.790799318912494}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -7.807664095523823}, {"token": "Find", "logprob": -8.193131624820698}, {"token": "<tool_call>", "logprob": -8.430628954532612}, {"token": "Use", "logprob": -8.780862032535541}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -8.899491488101948}, {"token": "#!/", "logprob": -9.165751635196674}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -9.239308535221088}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -9.589880167606342}, {"token": "B", "logprob": -9.603944002750385}, {"token": "That", "logprob": -9.816476999881733}]}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -0.0005777277566991756, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "bash", "logprob": -0.0005777277566991756}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -8.182622710666855}, {"token": " bash", "logprob": -9.08453539987584}, {"token": "sh", "logprob": -9.291122237644394}, {"token": "c", "logprob": -11.294160644016465}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -11.7432382