{"content": "# Gradient Descent and the Learning Rate\n\n## What Is Gradient Descent?\n\nGradient descent is an **iterative optimization algorithm** used to minimize a function (typically a loss/cost function) by moving in the direction of steepest descent, as defined by the negative gradient.\n\n### Core Idea\n\n1. **Compute the gradient** of the loss function with respect to the model parameters.\n2. **Update the parameters** in the opposite direction of the gradient.\n3. **Repeat** until convergence (or a stopping criterion is met).\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n\nFor a parameter $\\theta$ and loss function $J(\\theta)$:\n\n$$\n\\theta_{\\text{new}} = \\theta_{\\text{old}} - \\alpha \\nab", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.8891121516226015, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.8891121516226015}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -1.6192165980337343}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -2.172799743175336}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -2.28932539319975}, {"token": "Gradient", "logprob": -2.9938561091421327}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -3.0798699030874452}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -3.0873333582876406}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -3.7473503718374452}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -6.0405098567007265}, {"token": "Below", "logprob": -6.403604186534711}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -6.837279952525922}, {"token": "Explanation", "logprob": -7.480180419444867}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.5533577570913515}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -7.588124907970258}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -8.42755667066557}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -8.646557487010785}, {"token": "Under", "logprob": -8.777404464244672}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -8.85031286573393}, {"token": "Understanding", "logprob": -8.89440122938139}, {"token": "Grad", "logprob": -9.042392409801312}]}, {"token": " Gradient", "logprob": -0.019415243623647882, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " Gradient", "logprob": -0.019415243623647882}, {"token": " Understanding", "logprob": -4.033789022920523