{"content": "Here are the eight planets of our solar system, listed in order from the Sun, along with one interesting fact for each:\n\n1. **Mercury**  \n   *Fact:* A day on Mercury (from sunrise to sunrise) lasts about 176 Earth days, which is longer than its year (88 Earth days). This is due to its slow rotation and fast orbit.\n\n2. **Venus**  \n   *Fact:* Venus rotates in the opposite direction to most planets (retrograde rotation), meaning the Sun rises in the west and sets in the east. It is also the hottest planet due to its thick, carbon dioxide-rich atmosphere.\n\n3. **Earth**  \n   *Fact:* Earth is the only known planet with liquid water on its surface, and", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.0028933556084957957, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.0028933556084957957}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.11244764637998}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -7.949987319231543}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.455083754778418}, {"token": "Our", "logprob": -8.650495436907324}, {"token": "Note", "logprob": -9.033076194048437}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -9.18646231007627}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -9.206493285418066}, {"token": "Mer", "logprob": -9.585615065813574}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -9.60097303700498}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -9.637815383196386}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -9.885560897112402}, {"token": "Sure", "logprob": -10.157581237078222}, {"token": "Interesting", "logprob": -10.22732916188291}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -10.348590758562597}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -10.492615607500586}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.510135558367285}, {"token": " Here", "logprob": -10.709346678972754}, {"token": "Of", "logprob": -10.849256423235449}, {"token": "here", "logprob": -10.930020240068945}]}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.2511425813878816, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " are", "logprob": -0.2511425813878816}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -1.5059986910070222}, {"token": "\u2019s", "logprob": -8.532789309903507