{"content": "# How Hash Maps Handle Collisions\n\nA **hash map** stores key-value pairs in an array (the \"table\") where each key is mapped to an index via a **hash function**. Collisions occur when two different keys produce the same hash index. Here are the primary strategies for resolving them:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Separate Chaining\n\nEach bucket in the table holds a **linked list** (or another data structure) of all entries that hash to that index.\n\n```\nIndex:  0    1    2    3    4\n       [A]  [ ]  [B]->[C]  [D]\n```\n\n- **Insertion**: Compute hash \u2192 append to the list at that bucket.\n- **Lookup", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.7448108920992738, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.7448108920992738}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.8951881656588441}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -3.2881992587984925}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -3.756302667611969}, {"token": "Hash", "logprob": -3.8769043216647034}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.268765283578766}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -5.548912836069}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -5.5647400150240784}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -5.6197727451266175}, {"token": "Coll", "logprob": -5.809290719980133}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -5.875141931527985}, {"token": "When", "logprob": -6.071171594613922}, {"token": "Handling", "logprob": -6.145848108285797}, {"token": "Collision", "logprob": -6.772675348276032}, {"token": "Because", "logprob": -7.182642770761383}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.3109043369234925}, {"token": "How", "logprob": -7.534653497690094}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -7.578997446054352}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -7.643585992807282}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -8.002398324960602}]}, {"token": " How", "logprob": -0.06959191376735419, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " How", "logprob": -0.06959191376735419}, {"token": " Hash", "logprob": -2.9291690927224323}, {"token": " Collision", "logprob": -5.456810389109151}, {"token": " Handling", "logprob": -5.616394434519307}, {"tok