{"content": "Here is the water cycle described in four essential steps:\n\n1.  **Evaporation**: The sun heats water in oceans, lakes, and rivers, turning it into water vapor (gas). This vapor rises into the atmosphere.\n2.  **Condensation**: As the water vapor rises, it cools down and changes back into liquid water, forming tiny droplets that cluster together to create clouds.\n3.  **Precipitation**: When the water droplets in clouds become too heavy to remain suspended in the air, they fall back to Earth as rain, snow, sleet, or hail.\n4.  **Collection**: The water gathers in bodies of water such as oceans, lakes, and rivers, or soaks into the ground to replenish groundwater, ready to", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.5008087283077671, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.5008087283077671}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -1.1344509249630406}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -3.352706921667142}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -4.05642701444058}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.627355588048978}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -5.73268319425015}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.228014004797025}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -6.512302411169095}, {"token": "Although", "logprob": -7.121107113927884}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -7.1595010882320835}, {"token": " Here", "logprob": -7.385507596105619}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -7.571434987157865}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -7.575216305822416}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -7.632156384557767}, {"token": "Water", "logprob": -7.725713742345853}, {"token": "Actually", "logprob": -8.225078595251127}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -8.321617138952298}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -8.461866391271634}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -8.472407353490873}, {"token": "Certainly", "logprob": -8.6379594927731}]}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.09501676266419423, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " is", "logprob": -0.09501676266419423}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -2.406839653899546}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -8.246492