{"content": "The capital of Australia is **Canberra**.\n\n### Why isn't it Sydney?\n\nThe decision to make Canberra the capital, rather than Sydney or Melbourne, was the result of a political compromise during the federation of Australia in 1901. Here\u2019s the breakdown:\n\n1. **Political Rivalry**: Sydney (in New South Wales) and Melbourne (in Victoria) were the two largest and most influential cities at the time. Both states wanted the capital to be in their state to gain political and economic advantage.\n2. **The Compromise**: To prevent either state from dominating the others, the Constitution of Australia (Section 125) stipulated that the capital must be located in New South Wales but at least 100 miles (160 km", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0014477351959278906, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0014477351959278906}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -6.98931699789124}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -7.989496288662725}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -10.126813946133428}, {"token": "Actually", "logprob": -10.246271191006475}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -11.586134014492803}, {"token": "Capital", "logprob": -11.692541180020147}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -11.807291088467412}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -12.053557453518682}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -12.40533548391419}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -12.46568590200501}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -12.47674661672669}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -12.61652475393372}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -12.754324970608526}, {"token": "Yes", "logprob": -12.869567928677373}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -12.902675686245733}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -12.947953281765752}, {"token": "Contr", "logprob": -13.013039646511846}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -13.190784511929326}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -13.25542264974671}]}, {"token": " capital", "logprob": -0.0001138274158840602, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " capital", "logprob": -0.0001138274158840602}, {"token": " official", "logprob": 