{"content": "Inflation is a fundamental concept in macroeconomics that affects everyone from consumers to businesses. Here\u2019s a clear explanation of what it is and how central banks manage it.\n\n### What Is Inflation?\n\n**Inflation** is the rate at which the general level of prices for goods and services is rising, and, consequently, the purchasing power of currency is falling.\n\n- **Example**: If a loaf of bread cost $2 last year and costs $2.20 this year, the price has increased by 10%. If this happens across most goods and services, we say there is 10% inflation.\n- **Key Point**: Inflation is not just about one item getting more expensive (like a new iPhone model); it\u2019s about the *general* rise", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "In", "logprob": -0.7886336207562898, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "In", "logprob": -0.7886336207562898}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.9991095423871492}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -1.8053801417523836}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -5.188810622709415}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -5.844143188017032}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -6.266569411771915}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -6.54644612075629}, {"token": "Think", "logprob": -8.54039028884711}, {"token": "Understanding", "logprob": -9.108385360258243}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -9.131124770658634}, {"token": "At", "logprob": -9.515444076078555}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -10.2447703242475}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -10.443343436735294}, {"token": " inflation", "logprob": -10.559662139433048}, {"token": "Ex", "logprob": -10.570211684721134}, {"token": "Thinking", "logprob": -10.643724715726993}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -10.739980971830509}, {"token": "####", "logprob": -11.024883544462345}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -11.039955413358829}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -11.129476821439884}]}, {"token": "flation", "logprob": -0.0019155317876453637, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "flation", "logprob": -0.0019155317876453637}, {"token": " simple", "logprob": -7.7573209578